course: dictionary
lesson: 6248
title: A moderator keeps things fair and safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A moderator is a person whose job is to keep order. They make sure people follow the rules, take turns and stay safe. «Picture a TV debate as a game of tennis with words: two players, a referee called the moderator, and a clock.» The moderator is like the referee, so it must mean someone in charge of the rules.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. In a debate, the moderator asks questions and keeps time. In a game chat, the clue is in the brackets: «the game's moderators (the people who keep the chat safe) stop it.» So a moderator keeps the chat safe.
explain: Always test your meaning. Put it into the sentence: "the people who keep the chat safe stop it." That makes sense, so your meaning fits. If it does not make sense, look for another clue or check a dictionary.
fact: A moderator is a person who runs a discussion or debate and makes sure people follow the rules and take turns.
fact: A moderator can also check posts in an online forum or game chat and remove unkind or unsafe ones.
fact: A moderator can check that marks for exams are fair.
fact: In science, a moderator in a nuclear reactor slows down particles.
fact: «Real game staff and moderators never ask for your password.» If someone asks you for it, they are pretending, so tell a grown-up.
exercise: «Picture a TV debate as a game of tennis with words: two players, a referee called the moderator, and a clock.» In this picture, what does the moderator do? | *Keeps the rules and the time | Sings the national anthem | Plays on one of the teams | Hits the words back over the net
exercise: In a game chat, what does a moderator do? | Sends messages to players' parents | *Removes unkind or unsafe messages | Writes the rules for the game | Joins in with the chat to win
exercise: Mia asks what a moderator does with exams. What is the right answer? | *Checks that marks are fair | Gives out the prizes | Keeps the children quiet during the test | Reads out the questions to the class
test: «Real game staff and moderators never ask for your password.» What should you do if someone asks you for your password? | Tell them the password is "pizza" | Share it quickly so they stop asking | *Tell a grown-up and do not share it
test: In a school debate, what is the moderator's job? | *To ask questions, keep time and make sure people take turns | To write the speeches for both teams | To eat the snacks before the debate | To vote for the winning team
exam: Which sentence uses moderator to mean someone who removes unkind posts? | The moderator counted the goals at the match. | The moderator asked each team to take turns. | *The moderator removed the unkind posts from the forum.
